implementationPlan.description:
Extend scripts/tests/ci-workflows.test.mjs (task-669e6aff's split pin) with the R7 guard and the new placements. This is the last hunk of /mnt/d/moe-scratch/plan-5f5c/planned.diff; the dry-run copy is /mnt/d/moe-scratch/plan-5f5c/dry/scripts/tests/ci-workflows.test.mjs. Use your editing tool. The edits, in order:
1. Import readdirSync: `import { readdirSync, readFileSync } from 'node:fs';`.
2. Header: after the line 'These rows pin that split, ...', add `// R7 keeps every scripts/tests/*.test.mjs in one of the two, or in SKIP with the reason it runs nowhere.`
3. Before `// [command, the runner.os it runs on]`, add the two-line comment `// About 2 min on ubuntu-latest, 5-6 min under the two Windows PowerShells: Linux runs this pair per push,` / `// Windows only in the nightly.` and then `const AGENT_GUARDS = 'node --test scripts/tests/agent-git-guard.test.mjs scripts/tests/protected-agent-command.test.mjs';`. LONG gets `[AGENT_GUARDS, 'Windows'],` as its FIRST entry: R2 compares the nightly-only commands in file order, and the new nightly step comes before the three postflight ones.
4. FAST gets four entries after the parity-check.ps1 one: `[AGENT_GUARDS, 'Linux']`, `['bash scripts/tests/mention-provenance.sh', 'Linux']`, `['powershell -NoProfile -File scripts/tests/mention-provenance.ps1 -PowerShell powershell', 'Windows']` and `['pwsh -NoProfile -File scripts/tests/mention-provenance.ps1 -PowerShell pwsh', 'Windows']`.
5. After `const all = ...`, add `function runsOn(guard, os)` with its two-line comment, as in the diff. Only `runner.os == 'X'` and `runner.os != 'X'` restrict the OS. Any other guard (matrix.os) counts as every OS, which can only add owners, never hide one.
6. R2: the owners filter gains `&& runsOn(step.guard, os)`, because AGENT_GUARDS now sits in both a Linux PR step and a Windows nightly step. Add the per-file loop from the diff: for a LONG command that starts with `node --test `, no step that runs on that OS and is not nightly-only may name any of its files under any command line (message `${file} runs in PR CI on ${os}`). `nightlyOnly.length` goes from 3 to 4.
7. R3: retitle it 'R3: the fast launcher suites stay in PR CI on their OS' and add the same runsOn filter.
8. Append `const SKIP = {};` with its comment, then R7 'R7: every scripts/tests/*.test.mjs is run by a ci.yml step, or SKIP says why not', exactly as in the diff:
   - named: every whitespace token of every ci.yml run line that starts with `node --test `, in any job. A nightly-only step counts, because nightly.yml calls ci.yml.
   - files: readdirSync(new URL('.', import.meta.url)) filtered to *.test.mjs, asserting it includes ci-workflows.test.mjs.
   - deepEqual the unwired, unskipped list against [], with the message 'name each file in a ci.yml `node --test` step (a nightly-only step counts), or add it to SKIP with its reason'.
   - Each SKIP entry must name an existing file, must not also be wired, and needs a non-blank reason. Object.hasOwn keeps inherited Object keys out of the lookup.
SKIP stays empty, because all 7 suites pass on every engine CI runs them on. Its comment says a broken suite's reason names its fix row (DoD 1).
Test proof from planning: /mnt/d/moe-scratch/plan-5f5c/mutants.sh, run against the dry clone. All 7 rows pass on the edited tree, and 14 of 14 mutants fail the test:
   - a new unwired file;
   - a wired file dropped from its step;
   - the Linux pair's guard widened to run on Windows per push;
   - the Windows nightly guard without inputs.full;
   - either provenance step dropped;
   - a guard file added to the Windows PR doctor step, or to the helpers step, under another command line;
   - the nightly step deleted;
   - ci.yml reverted to e53f5a5c;
   - three bad SKIP entries (a wired file, a missing file, a blank reason).
The rows only read text, and no runtime code changes. Error handling: every assertion names the file or command it failed on, so a red run says what to wire or skip.

Verification: run the gate once, fresh, from the task worktree. The gate is executionContract checkRefs[0] && checkRefs[1], joined with ' && ' exactly as stored. Each ref is one parenthesized subshell, so the join is safe, and the governor's 19:10Z ruling makes the joined command the gate. Submit that command, its exit code and its output tail as the complete_task evidence. Planning ran it at e53f5a5c plus these edits, from a clone and from a simulated .worktrees/task-* worktree: EXIT 0 in 3m17s-3m22s, at load about 3 on 16 cores (the 20-min rail, DoD 6).
What it runs:
- ref0 (about 10 s):
  - the START time;
  - a PyYAML parse of every workflow ('YAML OK 5');
  - ci-workflows.test.mjs as a whole file (pass 7);
  - the 9 CI-reading rows of the other test files, counted to `9` as in task-669e6aff's gate;
  - the DoD 2 mutant: a temp copy of .github and scripts/tests plus an empty zz-unwired.test.mjs must FAIL ci-workflows.test.mjs, naming that file ('R7-MUTANT-KILLED').
- ref1 (about 3.3 min) runs three legs in parallel (DoD 6):
  - w1: CI's Windows PR commands under pwsh.exe, then node or powershell. That is the chain windows-latest uses: its step shell is pwsh, and a node.exe started straight from WSL would hide PSModulePath effects.
  - w2: the Windows nightly pair.
  - lx: CI's Linux commands, with a Linux pwsh 7 on PATH so that protected-agent-command's PowerShell 7 rows run as they will on ubuntu-latest.
  - Then it checks that no row skipped for a missing engine ('is not available on' / 'pwsh.exe not found'), that all three '@' leg markers are there, and that there are three provenance PASSED lines.
Expected tail, in order:
- END time;
- lx helpers: pass 73, fail 0;
- lx pair: pass 109, fail 0, skipped 6;
- 'mention-provenance.sh PASSED';
- w helpers: pass 71, skipped 2;
- doctor plus team: pass 11;
- two 'mention-provenance.ps1 PASSED' lines;
- w pair: pass 95, skipped 52.
The counts grow if a sibling row adds rows (task-c199e177 adds protected-agent-command rows). fail must be 0.
Linux pwsh: this host has none on PATH. The gate uses /tmp/hunt-9ca9/pwsh (PowerShell 7.6.9, extracted by hunt #25), else the copy at /mnt/d/moe-scratch/linux-pwsh-7.6.9, which survives a WSL restart and takes about 0.8 s per launch. If both are gone, the gate fails on 'pwsh is not available on linux'. Restore it with `cp -a` from any surviving copy, never a download.
Error handling for a red run: the output lists $L. Read $L/w1, $L/w2 and $L/lx there, and fix the cause, never the check.
- A row that fails in this task's own change: fix it.
- A newly wired suite that fails at W's base for a reason outside this row: fix it here only if the fix is a few clearly correct lines in that suite. Otherwise:
  - file a fix row with moe.create_task (evidence, failing rows, engine);
  - move the file from its ci.yml step into SKIP with a reason naming that row, and out of AGENT_GUARDS and FAST if it is there;
  - say so in the completion summary.
  Never wire a red suite (DoD 3).
- A timing-sensitive flake: rerun that leg's command alone once before acting.
QA re-run: the control checkout may hold another session's uncommitted edits. At planning it held the human's scripts/moe-agent.sh, which agent-git-guard, protected-agent-command and mention-provenance.sh all launch. If `git status --porcelain -- scripts .github CLAUDE.md docs` there is not empty, run the joined gate from a clone on D: detached at the completion sha:
```
git clone -q --shared --no-checkout . /mnt/d/moe-scratch/<dir>
git -C <dir> sparse-checkout set --no-cone '/*' '!/.moe/'
git -C <dir> checkout -q --detach <sha>
```
Then cd into <dir>. It must be on D: so the Windows legs can reach it. RED check: ref0 exits 1 at <sha>^ (no R7 there, so the unwired-file mutant passes), as it did at e53f5a5c in planning.
Do not run gh workflow run, change repository variables or touch rulesets. Name these follow-ups in the completion summary:
- the governor watches the first PR #230 run with this commit: the ubuntu and windows PR steps are green, and the Windows (nightly) step is skipped;
- the Windows pair's first real run is the next nightly, or `gh workflow run ci.yml --ref moe/work-2026-10-24 -f full=true` (the human's call).
